7. Swing \pard\sb400\sa150{\f0\fs28\b \u1057?\u1074?\u1080?\u1085?\u1075?}\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 Swing shifts the timing of off-beat steps slightly late, creating a "shuffle" feel. Rather than all steps being evenly spaced, the off-beats arrive a fraction later than expected.\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 In the Inspector settings, adjust the swing amount:\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  0% swing = perfectly straight, mechanical timing\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  ~30% swing = relaxed, human feel (hip-hop, lo-fi)\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  50%+ swing = pronounced shuffle (jazz, swing, some house music)\par
\pard\li720\sa200\f0\fs22\i Swing is subtle but powerful. A hip-hop beat with 30% swing feels relaxed and human. The same beat at 0% swing feels rigid.\par
8. Composition Exercise \pard\sb400\sa150{\f0\fs28\b \u1059?\u1087?\u1088?\u1072?\u1078?\u1085?\u1077?\u1085?\u1080?\u1077?: \u1087?\u1086?\u1083?\u1085?\u1072?\u1103? \u1082?\u1086?\u1084?\u1087?\u1086?\u1079?\u1080?\u1094?\u1080?\u1103?}\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 Compose a piece with at least three sections:\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 Section A (\u1050?\u1091?\u1087?\u1083?\u1077?\u1090?): A pattern with moderate density and a clear groove. Use the kick and snare as your anchors. Keep the hi-hat consistent but not overly busy. Apply velocity for natural dynamics.\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 Section B (\u1055?\u1088?\u1080?\u1087?\u1077?\u1074?): A fuller pattern with more energy. Consider adding more kick hits, denser hi-hats, or additional percussion layers. Raise the overall velocity slightly to create a sense of lift.\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 Transition: On the last bar of Section A, apply Note Repeat (\u215?4 or \u215?8) to the snare on steps 15\u8211?16. This creates a roll that propels the listener into the chorus.\par
\pard\sa200\f0\fs22 Additional considerations:\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  Apply velocity variation throughout \u8212? no flat dynamics\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  Add swing if the genre calls for it\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  Choose an appropriate drum kit for your genre\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  Use Chance on one or two secondary percussion elements\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sa100\f0\fs22 \bullet  Record each section and arrange them in Tracks View: A\u8211?A\u8211?B\u8211?B or A\u8211?B\u8211?A\u8211?B\par
